    Number of differences: 17571, average L1 error: 1.093529
    PASS!

--- vision/vision_passthrough ---

  make getwslpath=echo run  ->
    Load input image RANDOM and run passThrough
    Number of differences: 0, average L1 error: 0.000000
    PASS!

Byte-exact (0 differences) -- the tightest check of the four, as expected for a pure
passthrough with no pixel math in between.

--- ml/bottleneck (pure Python + torch reference, no CMake/OpenCV) ---

A real ResNet-family bottleneck block: conv1x1 -> conv3x3 -> conv1x1 with a skip
connection, built from mlir-aie's own kernels.conv2dk1/conv2dk3/conv2dk1_skip library
functions -- structurally the same building block this repo's own resnet50 pipeline
quantizes and runs, here as a hand-written kernel checked against a torch reference
instead of a quantized ONNX graph.

  make getwslpath=echo devicename=npu run_py  ->
    Avg NPU time: 1620us.
    PASS!

--- ml/conv2d (pure Python + torch reference) ---

1x1 conv, default shape (32x32, 64->64 channels), run twice: once plain, once with
--fuse_relu (both are separate cases in mlir-aie's own npu1 test matrix for this design).

  make getwslpath=echo devicename=npu run_py               -> Avg NPU time: 540us.  PASS!
  make getwslpath=echo devicename=npu fuse_relu=1 run_py    -> Avg NPU time: 533us.  PASS!

--- Conclusion ---

Seven more designs PASS on this machine's XDNA1 (Phoenix) NPU: all four vision/* designs
(the ones previously blocked by missing make/OpenCV) and three ml/* designs needing
torch for reference generation (bottleneck, conv2d plain, conv2d+fuse_relu). Combined
with the prior two logs, every mlir-aie programming_examples design tagged npu1
(Phoenix) that this survey identified as runnable without Strix-only hardware or a
substantial multi-file model (magika, mobilenet) has now been tried, and all of them
pass. bottleneck in particular is the closest thing in mlir-aie's own example set to this
repo's actual model family (a ResNet bottleneck block) -- still a hand-written kernel via
a separate toolchain, not a quantized ONNX graph through Quark/VitisAI EP, but the
closest structural match found so far.

New machine state beyond the two prior mlir-aie logs: `make` 4.4.1 in the mlir-aie-iron
conda env, OpenCV 5.0.0 at C:\Technical\thirdParty\opencv, torch 2.14.0+cpu in the
ironenv venv, a python3.exe shim in ironenv\Scripts. Nothing added to this repo's own 5
tracked conda envs.

Machine: Desktop 2 / Phoenix.
